    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d518-a1">

                <pb facs="0945" n="883" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg883"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 251.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gargiulo to Mr.
                            Maynard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Pera</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1878-05-20"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 20,
                    1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: The following is the account of the
                    plot against the Sultan, which I believe to be exact:</p>
                <p>This morning from five to six hundred men, armed with rifles and revolvers,
                    attacked the palace of Tcheragan, where the ex-Sultan Murad lives.</p>
                <p>The conspirators planned to carry off Murad and proclaim him Sultan. Notice of
                    the plot having been given, three thousand soldiers arrived and surrounded the
                    palace. The iron-clads also intercepted the approach to it by sea. All the
                    conspirators were disguised in the costume of refugees.</p>
                <p>There were found among them some officers of the army and some of the servants of
                    Murad. Murad is now at Top-Capon under a strong guard.</p>
                <p>It is asserted that about three hundred were killed and wounded on both sides.
                    The fight lasted three hours. Up to this time more than two hundred arrests have
                    been made, and they continue.</p>
                <p>The panic that prevailed at the bazaar existed also at Bechiktash. Patrols are
                    active everywhere.</p>
                <p>I am, sir,</p>
                <closer><signed>A. A. GARGIULO.</signed></closer>
            </div>
